infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title net/http vs a web framework: what each buys
  desc Since Go 1.22 the stdlib mux is the router — frameworks buy ergonomics, not routing
  compares
    - label net/http (stdlib)
      children
        - label One Handler interface
          desc ServeHTTP is the whole contract; muxes nest and middleware wraps uniformly
        - label HandlerFunc adapter
          desc Any function becomes a Handler with zero allocation
        - label 1.22 patterns
          desc Method, {id}, {path...}, {$} — what third-party routers existed for
        - label Most-specific-wins
          desc Order-independent; ambiguous routes panic at startup
        - label Routing under 1 microsecond
          desc Zero dependencies to audit
    - label Web framework
      children
        - label Binding and validation
          desc Parameter binding, content negotiation helpers
        - label Middleware and route groups
          desc Ecosystems and per-route middleware DSLs
        - label Regex route constraints
          desc Concrete features the stdlib mux genuinely lacks
        - label Non-standard signature
          desc A custom handler type every middleware must adapt to
        - label Dependency tree forever
          desc 47 transitive packages to audit; indirection over ResponseWriter
theme
  palette #6366f1 #f59e0b
